# SonarQube Code Quality

Project config: [`sonar-project.properties`](../../sonar-project.properties) (`bug-triage-langgraph`).

## When to run

Run SonarQube analysis **only** at these checkpoints:

- Before opening a PR (after significant code changes on a feature branch)
- When the user explicitly asks for a quality check, quality gate, or issue scan
- After fixing SonarQube-reported issues (to verify the fix)

Do **not** run analysis after every file edit, save, or small typo fix.

## How to invoke

### Via MCP (preferred in Cursor)

Requires the SonarQube plugin MCP server and `sonar auth login`. If tools are unavailable, tell the user to run the **sonar-integrate** skill and restart the session.

| Task | Skill / MCP tool |
|------|------------------|
| Analyze a file | `sonar-analyze` → `run_advanced_code_analysis` or `analyze_code_snippet` |
| Quality gate before PR | `sonar-quality-gate` → `get_project_quality_gate_status` |
| List open issues | `sonar-list-issues` (CLI: `sonar list issues -p bug-triage-langgraph`) |
| Fix a specific rule | `sonar-fix-issue` |
| Coverage gaps | `sonar-coverage` |
| Duplication | `sonar-duplication` |

Project key: `bug-triage-langgraph` (from `sonar-project.properties`).

### Via CLI (local full scan)

```bash
# One-time: install CLI + authenticate (see README)
sonar auth login -o <your-org-key>

# Full project scan from repo root
sonar scan
```

### Via CI

GitHub Actions runs on push to `main` and on PRs — see [`.github/workflows/sonarqube.yml`](../../.github/workflows/sonarqube.yml). Requires `SONAR_TOKEN` and `SONAR_HOST_URL` repo secrets.

## Setup (one-time)

1. Install [sonarqube-cli](https://cli.sonarqube.com/) (`irm ... | iex` on Windows)
2. Authenticate: `sonar auth login -o <org-key>` (EU) or `-s https://sonarqube.us` (US)
3. Create project `bug-triage-langgraph` in SonarCloud (or link via GitHub integration)
4. Add GitHub secrets: `SONAR_TOKEN`, `SONAR_HOST_URL` (`https://sonarcloud.io` for SonarCloud)
5. Restart Cursor so SonarQube MCP tools load
